NNAAMMEE
       pam_ftp - PAM module for anonymous access module

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaamm__ffttpp..ssoo [debug] [ignore] [users=_X_X_X_,_Y_Y_Y_,...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       pam_ftp is a PAM module which provides a pluggable anonymous ftp mode
       of access.

       This module intercepts the user's name and password. If the name is _f_t_p
       or _a_n_o_n_y_m_o_u_s, the user's password is broken up at the _@ delimiter into
       a _P_A_M___R_U_S_E_R and a _P_A_M___R_H_O_S_T part; these pam-items being set
       accordingly. The username (_P_A_M___U_S_E_R) is set to _f_t_p. In this case the
       module succeeds. Alternatively, the module sets the _P_A_M___A_U_T_H_T_O_K item
       with the entered password and fails.

       This module is not safe and easily spoofable.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       ddeebbuugg
           Print debug information.

       iiggnnoorree
           Pay no attention to the email address of the user (if supplied).

       ffttpp==_X_X_X_,_Y_Y_Y_,_._._.
           Instead of _f_t_p or _a_n_o_n_y_m_o_u_s, provide anonymous login to the comma
           separated list of users: _X_X_X_,_Y_Y_Y_,_._._.. Should the applicant enter
           one of these usernames the returned username is set to the first in
           the list: _X_X_X.

MMOODDUULLEE TTYYPPEESS PPRROOVVIIDDEEDD
       Only the aauutthh module type is provided.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
       PAM_SUCCESS
